-- Synthetic rows for the D1 import fixture (WP10): every table of the Worker's
-- schema, shaped like what D1 really holds: TEXT UUIDs, the Worker's
-- `...T10:00:00.123Z` timestamps next to SQLite's `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`, the
-- literal default text where a column was left out of an INSERT, JSON weekday
-- arrays, the Worker's stop kinds. Dates that matter to the app are relative to
-- the day the SQL runs, so the fixture never goes stale.
--
-- Valid against the Worker's migrations 0000-0009 with foreign keys ON (the
-- parity harness loads the same file into a local D1). Rows the Rust schema
-- cannot hold are deliberate and listed in tests/wp10_import.rs.
-- Load order: 0000-0009, seed_cf.sql, this file.
BEGIN TRANSACTION;

-- users: a Worker PBKDF2 hash, Argon2, a guest, OAuth, a bot, default-literal timestamps

-- user_roles (the second worker row has no unique constraint in D1)

-- refresh tokens: the Worker's own (tests/fixtures/wp6_ref_auth.json) and a revoked one

-- verification codes, notifications, posts, push devices, audit log, staff presence

-- a brand on top of seed_cf.sql's three

-- addresses: two stations, a middle stop, one without a longitude

-- a route with pickup points and pictures (one without a thumbnail, one without a size)

-- a four-seat layout (valid JSON) and a layout whose JSON is broken

-- schedules: JSON weekday arrays (Sunday = 1), a mask, no mask

-- trips: one with a seat inventory and a drifted counter, one without inventory, one past

-- bookings and what hangs off them

-- promotions: a legacy campaign, a tiered campaign, its coupons

-- reviews: comma-separated and JSON tags, a pending one, one for a booking that is gone

-- support chat: two messages in one second, two assignment rows, an exchange pointing at a message that is gone

-- ads, jobs, alerts

-- places with an OSM id (the seed's have none and the app requires one)

COMMIT;
